:R-HSA-2151201  a           owl:NamedIndividual , obo:GO_0008150 ;
        rdfs:comment        "Phosphorylated PPARGC1A (PGC-1alpha) does not bind DNA directly but instead interacts with other transcription factors, notably NRF1 and NRF2 (via HCF1). NRF1 and NRF2 together with PPARGC1A activate the transcription of nuclear-encoded, mitochondrially targeted proteins such as TFB2M, TFB1M, and TFAM. PGC-1beta and PPRC appear to act similarly to PGC-1alpha but have not been as well studied. Transcription of PPARGC1A itself is upregulated by CREB1 (in response to calcium), MEF2C/D, ATF2, and PPARGC1A. Transcription of PPARGC1A is repressed by NR1D1 (REV-ERBA)." ;
        rdfs:label          "Transcriptional activation of mitochondrial biogenesis" ;
        dc:contributor      "Authored: May, B, 2012-02-27" , "Reviewed: Lezza, Angela M S, 2013-12-07" , "Edited: May, B, 2012-02-27" , "GOC:reactome_curators" ;
        dc:date             "2023-06-21" ;
        pav:providedBy      "https://reactome.org" ;
        oboInOwl:hasDbXref  "R-HSA-2151201" ;
        skos:narrower       <http://model.geneontology.org/R-HSA-1592230/R-HSA-1592230> ;
        skos:note           "org.biopax.paxtools.model.level3.Pathway" .

